.subckt pw4_clamp a ref en vss
* holds a at REF while en is high
XCL a en ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_bridge a b ref dac we clamp vdd vss
* Programmable resistor, BRIDGE across an edge (z bus to f bus), 0 to 2.5 uS: raises the weight.
* LVT PMOS in series between a and b with one gate gn (the stored node) and one well (mid). gn is written from the DAC
* line while a, b and the well are held at REF (the buses' clamps and XCLM); afterwards it floats and rides on the
* terminals through its two capacitors. The conductance falls as the code rises; above about 1.1 V it is zero.
* Writer, in two stages as in the bias word: at the gate a 5 V NMOS (passes codes up to 0.6 to 0.8 V) beside an LVT
* PMOS (passes the codes above, so the resistor can be shut off at every corner); then a transmission gate to the DAC
* line. When not writing, the node between the stages (wm) is held at REF: the stored gate has REF behind its off
* writer whatever the DAC line does. The hold (XWC) is a long, weak NMOS on purpose: if the transmission gate to the
* DAC line ever failed shorted, REF would see at most a microampere from the DAC pin, not 80.
XPA a gn ma mid sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=2 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XPA2 ma gn mid mid sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=2 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XPB2 mb gn mid mid sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=2 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XPB b gn mb mid sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=2 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XCA gn a sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=10.99 L=10.99 MF=1 m=1
XCB gn b sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=10.99 L=10.99 MF=1 m=1
XW1N gn we wm vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 L=4 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW1P gn we_b wm vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=1 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW2 wm dac we we_b vdd vss cd_tg_small
XWC wm we_b ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=8 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XWI we we_b vdd vss cmos_inv
XCLM mid clamp ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_shunt a b ref dac we clamp vdd vss
* Programmable resistor, SHUNT from an edge's midpoint bus to REF, 0 to 20 uS: lowers the weight.
* LVT PMOS in series between a and b with one gate gn (the stored node) and one well (mid). gn is written from the DAC
* line while a, b and the well are held at REF (the buses' clamps and XCLM); afterwards it floats and rides on the
* terminals through its two capacitors. The conductance falls as the code rises; above about 1.1 V it is zero.
* Writer, in two stages as in the bias word: at the gate a 5 V NMOS (passes codes up to 0.6 to 0.8 V) beside an LVT
* PMOS (passes the codes above, so the resistor can be shut off at every corner); then a transmission gate to the DAC
* line. When not writing, the node between the stages (wm) is held at REF: the stored gate has REF behind its off
* writer whatever the DAC line does. The hold (XWC) is a long, weak NMOS on purpose: if the transmission gate to the
* DAC line ever failed shorted, REF would see at most a microampere from the DAC pin, not 80.
XPA a gn mid mid sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=2 W=8 nf=1 ad=4.64 as=4.64 pd=32.58 ps=32.58 nrd=0.01812 nrs=0.01812 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=2 m=2
XPB b gn mid mid sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=2 W=8 nf=1 ad=4.64 as=4.64 pd=32.58 ps=32.58 nrd=0.01812 nrs=0.01812 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=2 m=2
XCA gn a sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=10.99 L=10.99 MF=1 m=1
XCB gn b sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=10.99 L=10.99 MF=1 m=1
XW1N gn we wm vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 L=4 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW1P gn we_b wm vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=1 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW2 wm dac we we_b vdd vss cd_tg_small
XWC wm we_b ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=8 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XWI we we_b vdd vss cmos_inv
XCLM mid clamp ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_mid m1 m2 b1 b2 iso vss
* The two midpoints' isolation switches (one cell between the two hidden-to-output resistor pairs): midpoint to its bus.
XSW1 m1 iso b1 vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSW2 m2 iso b2 vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_nrn_h y p q bus qs dn iso vss
* A hidden neuron's west cell: four switches and three unit strips. y is the neuron's wire (f1 or f2).
*   XSWB  isolation switch: the wire y to its bus
*   XSWD  the damping network's switch (revision 7): the wire y to dn, a second finger of XSWB on the same diffusion
*         of the wire (each finger has 0.58 um2 and 4.29 um of it); its unit and plate are in the east cell
*   XSW4, XU1..XU3  the helper beside R4: switch AT THE WIRE, then three units in series to p (400 kohm, 2.5 uS)
*   XSW7  the switch of the helper beside R7: q to qs; its three units are the east cell (pw4_units3d), qs to REF
XSWB y iso bus vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=1.16 pd=4.29 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSWD y iso dn vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=1.16 pd=4.29 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSW4 y iso n1 vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XU1 n1 n2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU2 n2 n3 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU3 n3 p vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XSW7 q iso qs vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_units3d a b dn vss
* A hidden neuron's east cell (revision 7): the three units of the helper beside R7, from its switch to REF (a to b),
* and the damping network behind the west cell's XSWD: one unit from dn, then the plate to REF (b), lower plate on REF.
* In programmed mode the network lies from the wire to REF: above 1/(2 pi R C) it lowers the first amplifier's feedback
* factor, so its loop crosses over lower; it has no path at DC. In fixed mode XSWD is off and only its finger is on y.
XU1 a n2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU2 n2 n3 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU3 n3 b vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU4 dn dc vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XCD dc b sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=23.1 L=10.4 MF=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_nrn_z y p q bus qs nm ref iso vss
* The output neuron's west cell: four switches in a row and three unit strips. y is the neuron's wire (z).
*   XSWB  isolation switch: the wire y to its bus
*   XSW4, XU1  the helper beside R4: switch at the wire (three 4 um fingers), one unit to p (133 kohm, 7.5 uS)
*   XSW7  the switch of the helper beside R7 (three fingers): q to qs. XU2, XU3: one of its two branches, two units in
*         series from qs to REF; the other branch is in the east cell (pw4_units5)
*   XSZ   the DAC edge's switch at the wire: y to nm; its strips are in the east cell
XSWB y iso bus vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSW4 y iso n1 vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=3 m=3
XU1 n1 p vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XSW7 q iso qs vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=3 m=3
XU2 qs n2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU3 n2 ref vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XSZ y iso nm vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_units5 nm nd qs ref vss
* The output neuron's east cell: five strips.
*   XU1..XU3  the DAC edge, nm to nd. The third strip is shorter than a unit by what the pin resistor, the board and the
*             edge's two switches add, so that the whole edge from ua[1] to z is three units (less the 0.2% that the output
*             neuron's helpers lose in their own switches).
*   XU4, XU5  the second branch of the helper beside R7: two units in series from qs to REF
XU1 nm n2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU2 n2 n3 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU3 n3 nd vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=122300
XU4 qs n4 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XU5 n4 ref vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
.ends

.subckt pw4_dacgate nd dac ref iso vdd vss
* The DAC edge's gate, in the output neuron: nd -- transmission gate -- DAC line -- (pin resistor) -- ua[1].
* iso high: (V_DAC - REF) x 0.25 is added to the output neuron's drive (its bank is matched for this edge, so there is
* no spring): the output bias, and the nudge. iso low: nd is held at REF (XCL), so the switch on z has REF behind the
* strips and the DAC line cannot reach z whatever its voltage. `off` is made here from `iso`.
XCL nd off ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_03v3_nvt L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSD nd dac iso off vdd vss transmission_gate UNITS=8
XOFF iso off vdd vss cmos_inv
.ends

.subckt pw4_rblock4 f1x f2x zx m1x m2x ref dac we0 we1 we2 we3 clampw vdd vss
* The row of the four programmable resistors with the five buses' clamps.
XBCL_f1 f1x ref clampw vss pw4_clamp
XBCL_f2 f2x ref clampw vss pw4_clamp
XBCL_z zx ref clampw vss pw4_clamp
XBCL_m1 m1x ref clampw vss pw4_clamp
XBCL_m2 m2x ref clampw vss pw4_clamp
XSH1 m1x ref ref dac we0 clampw vdd vss pw4_shunt
XSH2 m2x ref ref dac we1 clampw vdd vss pw4_shunt
XBR1 zx f1x ref dac we2 clampw vdd vss pw4_bridge
XBR2 zx f2x ref dac we3 clampw vdd vss pw4_bridge
.ends

.subckt pw4_pulldown a vdd vss
* weak pull-down: a long 5 V NMOS with its gate at the supply
XPD a vdd vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 L=8 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt pw4_tg a b en en_b vdd vss
* a transmission gate of 0.5 um transistors: it leaks far less when off than the 0.15 um ones
XMN a en b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XMP a en_b b vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=2.32 as=2.32 pd=16.58 ps=16.58 nrd=0.03625 nrs=0.03625 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=2 m=2
.ends

.subckt pw4_bias_word dac line we bp bp_b nref pref ref vdd vss
* One stored bias. XF is a PMOS follower: gate sg (the stored node), source = the read line, which goes to the
* EXTERNAL input of the accepted bias switch.
* Idle (bp low, we low): the DAC line is on the read line through XDL, so the accepted external-bias function is
*   unchanged; every current source is off and nothing flows.
* Write (we high, bp low): the DAC holds the line. The sink XIS pulls the read current through the follower and the
*   writer (XW1N, XW1P, XW2) joins the follower's drain to its gate, so the gate takes the value that puts the line at
*   the DAC voltage at the read current. XTW returns the same current to the line, so none flows in the DAC pin.
* Read (bp high): the DAC is off the line, the drain is grounded (XRD) and the top source XIT feeds the line (XTS).
* Not writing: the writer's middle node wm is held at REF (XWC), so the off writer has REF on its far side.
XF drn sg line line sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=1 W=10 nf=1 ad=11.6 as=11.6 pd=80.58 ps=80.58 nrd=0.00725 nrs=0.00725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=4 m=4
XST sg ref sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=10.99 L=10.99 MF=1 m=1
XW1N sg we wm vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 L=1 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW1P sg we_b wm vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=1 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW2 wm drn we we_b vdd vss cd_tg_small
XWC wm ref we_b we vdd vss cd_tg_small
XWI we we_b vdd vss cmos_inv
XIT top pref vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L=2 W=2 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=0.58 pd=4.58 ps=4.58 nrd=0.145 nrs=0.145 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XTS line bp_b top vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XTW line we_b top vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XIS tail nref vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=1 W=2 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=0.58 pd=4.58 ps=4.58 nrd=0.145 nrs=0.145 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSS drn we tail vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XRD drn bp vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XDL dac line bp_b bp vdd vss pw4_tg
.ends

.subckt pw4_bias dac bw1 bw2 e1 e2 bias_prog write ref vdd vss
* The bias block: the two bias words, their own current reference (a resistor into a diode; nothing hangs on the
* chip's vbn), the gating of their two write strobes and the pull-downs of BIAS_PROG and WRITE.
* A bias word is written while WRITE and its external-bias enable (e1 = uio[0], e2 = uio[1]) are high and BIAS_PROG is
* low. The block makes its own inverse of WRITE (the decoder in the strip has another).
XIWB write nwrite vdd vss cmos_inv
XIE1 e1 ne1 vdd vss cmos_inv
XIE2 e2 ne2 vdd vss cmos_inv
XB1 nwrite ne1 bias_prog wb1 vdd vss cmos_nor3
XB2 nwrite ne2 bias_prog wb2 vdd vss cmos_nor3
XBPB bias_prog bp_b vdd vss cmos_inv
XBP bp_b bp vdd vss cmos_inv
XPD4 bias_prog vdd vss pw4_pulldown
XPD5 write vdd vss pw4_pulldown
XRREF vdd nref vss pdk_rbias2_v RVALUE=286k
XMREF nref nref vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=1 W=2 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=0.58 pd=4.58 ps=4.58 nrd=0.145 nrs=0.145 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=8 m=8
XMN0 pref nref vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=1 W=2 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=0.58 pd=4.58 ps=4.58 nrd=0.145 nrs=0.145 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XMP0 pref pref vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L=2 W=2 nf=1 ad=0.58 as=0.58 pd=4.58 ps=4.58 nrd=0.145 nrs=0.145 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW1 dac bw1 wb1 bp bp_b nref pref ref vdd vss pw4_bias_word
XW2 dac bw2 wb2 bp bp_b nref pref ref vdd vss pw4_bias_word
.ends

.subckt pw4_decoder a0 a1 write res_sel weight_prog we0 we1 we2 we3 iso clampw vdd vss
XIW write nwrite vdd vss cmos_inv
XIA0 a0 na0 vdd vss cmos_inv
XIA1 a1 na1 vdd vss cmos_inv
* gw: writing a resistor word is allowed (WRITE high, RES_SEL high, WEIGHT_PROG low); ngw high keeps every strobe low
XIRS res_sel nrs vdd vss cmos_inv
XGW nwrite nrs weight_prog gw vdd vss cmos_nor3
XGWB gw ngw vdd vss cmos_inv
XD0 a0 a1 ngw we0 vdd vss cmos_nor3
XD1 na0 a1 ngw we1 vdd vss cmos_nor3
XD2 a0 na1 ngw we2 vdd vss cmos_nor3
XD3 na0 na1 ngw we3 vdd vss cmos_nor3
* clampw (to the many clamps) and iso (to the switches) each come from the pin through their own gates:
* clampw stuck either way cannot turn a switch on
XWPB weight_prog clampw vdd vss cmos_inv
XWN weight_prog nwp vdd vss cmos_inv
XWP nwp iso vdd vss cmos_inv
XPD6 res_sel vdd vss pw4_pulldown
XPD7 weight_prog vdd vss pw4_pulldown
.ends

.subckt native_six_network reset hold_in bias1 bias2 vbn ref pad vdd vss obs_sel0 obs_sel1 obs_sel2 pad2 obs2_sel0 obs2_sel1 f1 f2 z p1 q1 p2 q2 pz qz m1 m2 observed_a observed_b weak weak_b  CORE_MATCH=1 READ_MATCH=1
*.iopin f1
*.iopin f2
*.iopin z
*.iopin p1
*.iopin q1
*.iopin p2
*.iopin q2
*.iopin pz
*.iopin qz
*.iopin m1
*.iopin m2
*.iopin reset
*.iopin hold_in
*.iopin bias1
*.iopin bias2
*.iopin vbn
*.iopin ref
*.iopin pad
*.iopin vdd
*.iopin vss
*.iopin obs_sel0
*.iopin obs_sel1
*.iopin obs_sel2
*.iopin pad2
*.iopin obs2_sel0
*.iopin obs2_sel1
XACT1 h1 ref natural1 ref vbn vdd vss lean_act
XACT2 ref h2 natural2 ref vbn vdd vss lean_act
XH1 natural1 bias1 reset hold_in f1 h1 ref vdd vss p1 q1 weak weak_b native_res_hold_state DPROG=0.5
XH2 natural2 bias2 reset hold_in f2 h2 ref vdd vss p2 q2 weak weak_b native_res_hold_state DPROG=0.5
XZ hz ref reset hold_in z hz ref vdd vss pz qz weak weak_b native_res_hold_state DPROG=1
XREAD net1 pad vdd vss xor_readout MATCH={READ_MATCH}
XRW4 z f1 vss m1 pdk_rfixed2_h_m RVALUE=200k
XRW5 z f2 vss m2 pdk_rfixed2_h_m RVALUE=200k
XOBS z h1 h2 ref f1 f2 observed_a observed_b obs_sel0 obs_sel1 obs_sel2 vdd vss net1 observe_mux
XOBS2 ref z h1 h2 obs2_sel0 obs2_sel1 vdd vss obs2 second_observer
XREAD2 obs2 pad2 reset ref vdd vss second_readout
.ends

* The external pin names and the calibrated shunt/bridge addresses are the frozen design's.
* bit_a,bit_b select a row ONLY when a resistor write is strobed.
.subckt native_bank_enable bit_a bit_b we0 we1 we2 we3 z0 z1 z2 z3 a0 a1 a2 a3 b0 b1 b2 b3 vdd vss
XIA bit_a nba vdd vss cmos_inv
XIB bit_b nbb vdd vss cmos_inv
XZ bit_a bit_b sel_z vdd vss cmos_nor2
XA nba bit_b sel_a vdd vss cmos_nor2
XB bit_a nbb sel_b vdd vss cmos_nor2
XNZ sel_z nz vdd vss cmos_inv
XNA sel_a na vdd vss cmos_inv
XNB sel_b nb vdd vss cmos_inv
XI0 we0 nw0 vdd vss cmos_inv
XI1 we1 nw1 vdd vss cmos_inv
XI2 we2 nw2 vdd vss cmos_inv
XI3 we3 nw3 vdd vss cmos_inv
XZ0 nz nw0 z0 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XZ1 nz nw1 z1 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XZ2 nz nw2 z2 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XZ3 nz nw3 z3 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XA0 na nw0 a0 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XA1 na nw1 a1 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XA2 na nw2 a2 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XA3 na nw3 a3 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XB0 nb nw0 b0 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XB1 nb nw1 b1 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XB2 nb nw2 b2 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XB3 nb nw3 b3 vdd vss cmos_nor2
.ends

* The native R3 is 200k into each neuron. In six-edge mode its far end
* is connected to REF through the corresponding series resistor below.
* The second branch goes from p to switched VSS. Together they reproduce
* the old 5 uS bias input at a fixed -REF/12 or -7 REF/36 offset.
.subckt native_fixed_offsets ref bias1 bias2 p1 p2 six vss ret1 ret2
* version 4: H1 trim as H2 (48.28 kohm, was 18.18 kohm), so that p1 still sees 5.000 uS
XR1 ref bias1 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=48275.86207
XR2 ref bias2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=48275.86207
* version 4: H1 chain as H2 (4 x 257142.85714 ohm = 1.029 Mohm, was 8 x 300k = 2.4 Mohm)
XG11 p1 a1 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG12 a1 a2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG13 a2 a3 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG14 a3 end1 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG21 p2 b1 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG22 b1 b2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG23 b2 b3 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
XG24 b3 end2 vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=257142.85714
* variant: the sources of the two mode switches go to ret1, ret2 (the programmable transistors below them)
XRETURN end1 end2 ret1 ret2 six vss native_ground_return
.ends

* One buffered raw input feeds the common end of two native 200k resistor pairs.
* Each hidden end has its own isolation switch. A floating common end would
* leave a DC connection between H1 and H2 in the original operating mode.
.subckt native_clamped_row raw raw_bus f1 f2 ref dac we0 we1 we2 we3 six park vdd vss
XEND f1 f2 leaf1 leaf2 six vss pw4_mid
XR1 raw leaf1 vss mid1 pdk_rfixed2_h_m RVALUE=200k
XR2 raw leaf2 vss mid2 pdk_rfixed2_h_m RVALUE=200k
XMID mid1 mid2 mx1 mx2 six vss pw4_mid
XLEAF_BUS leaf1 leaf2 fx1 fx2 six vss pw4_mid
XRB fx1 fx2 raw_bus mx1 mx2 ref dac we0 we1 we2 we3 park vdd vss pw4_rblock4
.ends

* A hidden endpoint has three incident programmed edges. The two new edges
* add 15 uS nominal, on top of the original 17.5 uS feedback at both R4/R7.
.subckt native_hidden_feedback f p q ref six vss
XSW1 f q sw4 sw7 six vss pw4_mid
XSW2 f q sw4 sw7 six vss pw4_mid
XSW3 f q sw4 sw7 six vss pw4_mid
XR4A sw4 p vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XR4B sw4 p vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XR7A sw7 ref vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
XR7B sw7 ref vss pdk_rbias2 RVALUE=133333
.ends

