* ---- v4 additions, one instance per layout cell
XMID m1 m2 m1x m2x iso vss pw4_mid
XNH1 f1 p1 q1 f1x qs1 dn1 iso vss pw4_nrn_h
XUE1 qs1 ref dn1 vss pw4_units3d
XNH2 f2 p2 q2 f2x qs2 dn2 iso vss pw4_nrn_h
XUE2 qs2 ref dn2 vss pw4_units3d
XNZ z pz qz zx qsz nm ref iso vss pw4_nrn_z
XUZ nm nd qsz ref vss pw4_units5
XDG nd ext_in ref iso vdd vss pw4_dacgate
XRB f1x f2x zx m1x m2x ref ext_in z0 z1 z2 z3 clampw vdd vss pw4_rblock4
XDEC obs_sel2 obs2_sel0 write res_filtered weight_prog we0 we1 we2 we3 iso clampw vdd vss pw4_decoder
XBW ext_in bw1 bw2 ext_en1 ext_en2 bias_prog write ref vdd vss pw4_bias
* In six-edge mode the two original unity buffers drive raw A and B.
* In original operation they feed each hidden R3 and the readout as before.
XNBP bias_prog nbp vdd vss cmos_inv
XNE1 ext_en1 ne1 vdd vss cmos_inv
XNE2 ext_en2 ne2 vdd vss cmos_inv
XARM nbp ne1 ne2 armed vdd vss cmos_nor3
XNARM armed narmed vdd vss cmos_inv
XMODE narmed clampw six vdd vss cmos_nor2
XPARK six park vdd vss cmos_inv
XRCIN_R res_sel res_filtered vss sky130_fd_pr__res_xhigh_po_0p35 L=6.90 mult=1 m=1
XRCIN_C res_filtered vss sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=15.7 L=15.7 MF=1 m=1
XRESERVOIR1 ref vss sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=15.7 L=15.7 MF=1 m=1
XRESERVOIR2 ref vss sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=15.7 L=15.7 MF=1 m=1
XRWEAK_N weak_src weak vss sky130_fd_pr__res_xhigh_po_0p35 L=69.90 mult=1 m=1
XRWEAK_P weak_b_src weak_b vss sky130_fd_pr__res_xhigh_po_0p35 L=69.90 mult=1 m=1
XGATELOAD weak_b vss sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=8.97 L=8.97 MF=1 m=1
XHOLD_AND_B res_filtered six vss vss vdd vdd weak_b_src sky130_fd_sc_hd__nand2_1
XHOLD_AND weak_b_src weak_src vdd vss cmos_inv
* Two sets of eight native switches select the fixed or legacy H bias branches.
XSEL_RAW1 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED1 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW2 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED2 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW3 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED3 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW4 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED4 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW5 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED5 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW6 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED6 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW7 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED7 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSEL_RAW8 bias1 bias2 h1bias h2bias park vss pw4_mid
XSEL_FIXED8 fixed1 fixed2 h1bias h2bias six vss pw4_mid
XSTATIC ref fixed1 fixed2 p1 p2 six vss ret1 ret2 native_fixed_offsets
XENABLE bit_a bit_b we0 we1 we2 we3 z0 z1 z2 z3 a0 a1 a2 a3 b0 b1 b2 b3 vdd vss native_bank_enable
XCLAMP_BUS bias1 bias2 ax bx six vss pw4_mid
XROW_A bias1 ax f1 f2 ref ext_in a0 a1 a2 a3 six park vdd vss native_clamped_row
XROW_B bias2 bx f1 f2 ref ext_in b0 b1 b2 b3 six park vdd vss native_clamped_row
XH1FEEDBACK f1 p1 q1 ref six vss native_hidden_feedback
XH2FEEDBACK f2 p2 q2 ref six vss native_hidden_feedback
* ---- variant: programmable hidden offsets (takeover/bias/SPEC.md), one instance per new layout cell
XOPROG ret1 ret2 bg1 bg2 vss native_offset_prog
XOWORD1 bg1 ext_in bstb1 ref vdd vss native_offset_word
XOWORD2 bg2 ext_in bstb2 ref vdd vss native_offset_word
XOSTROBE bit_a bit_b we0 we1 bstb1 bstb2 vdd vss native_offset_strobe
.ends

.subckt native_ground_return m1 m2 b1 b2 iso vss
XSW1 m1 iso b1 vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XSW2 m2 iso b2 vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=0.5 W=4 nf=1 ad=1.16 as=1.16 pd=8.58 ps=8.58 nrd=0.0725 nrs=0.0725 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

* ==== Programmable hidden offsets (variant v3 of 2026-11-23, takeover/bias/SPEC.md); everything below is new ====

.subckt native_offset_prog ret1 ret2 bg1 bg2 vss
* The pair of programmable offset transistors. Each sits between the source of the existing mode switch (XSW_k of
* native_ground_return, gate six) and ground: end_k -- XSW_k -- ret_k -- XPROG_k -- vss. Gate bg_k = the stored word;
* source and body on the same ground as the storage capacitor, so the stored voltage is the gate-to-source voltage.
* Long-channel 1.8 V NMOS: with bg_k at the supply the chain draws today's current; lower bg_k lowers the offset.
* version 4: XPROG1 the size of XPROG2 (W 1, L 3.5; was W 0.42, L 3.2)
XPROG1 ret1 bg1 vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=3.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XPROG2 ret2 bg2 vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=3.5 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
.ends

.subckt native_offset_word bg dac bstb ref vdd vss
* One stored hidden offset (two instances): the stored gate bg on a MIM to the local ground, and a copy of the
* two-stage writer of pw4_shunt, device for device. At bg a 5 V NMOS (XW1N) beside an LVT PMOS (XW1P), then a
* transmission gate (XW2) to the DAC line; when not writing, the middle node wm is held at REF by the long weak
* NMOS XWC, so the stored gate has REF behind its off writer whatever the DAC line does. XWI: the strobe's inverter
* (bstbb). Stored node on the MIM's first terminal (top plate), as in the existing words. No clamp on bg.
XC bg vss sky130_fd_pr__cap_mim_m3_1 W=8.97 L=8.97 MF=1 m=1
XW1N bg bstb wm vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 L=4 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW1P bg bstbb wm vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_lvt L=1 W=1 nf=1 ad=0.29 as=0.29 pd=2.58 ps=2.58 nrd=0.29 nrs=0.29 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XW2 wm dac bstb bstbb vdd vss cd_tg_small
XWC wm bstbb ref vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L=8 W=0.42 nf=1 ad=0.1218 as=0.1218 pd=1.42 ps=1.42 nrd=0.6905 nrs=0.6905 sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 mult=1 m=1
XWI bstb bstbb vdd vss cmos_inv
.ends

.subckt native_offset_strobe bit_a bit_b we0 we1 bstb1 bstb2 vdd vss
* The two strobes of the bias row, built beside the stored words from global nets (layout/INTERFACE.md).
* Row (bit_a, bit_b) = (1, 1), unused by the resistor rows; we0 (word address 0) writes H1's offset, we1 (word
* address 1) H2's. we0, we1 come from pw4_decoder and already contain WRITE, RES_SEL, not WEIGHT_PROG and the word
* address, so six = 0 whenever bstb1 or bstb2 is high.
*   bstb1 = bit_a & bit_b & we0 = NOR2(NAND2(bit_a, bit_b), not we0);  bstb2 likewise with we1
XSAB bit_a bit_b vss vss vdd vdd nab sky130_fd_sc_hd__nand2_1
XSW0 we0 nwe0 vdd vss cmos_inv
XSW1 we1 nwe1 vdd vss cmos_inv
XSB1 nab nwe0 bstb1 vdd vss cmos_nor2
XSB2 nab nwe1 bstb2 vdd vss cmos_nor2
.ends
